\DOC ASSERT_CONCL_TAC

\TYPE {ASSERT_CONCL_TAC : term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Checks that the goal's conclusion is the supplied term, leaving the goal
unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
Takes one argument {t : term}, which is compared against the goal's conclusion.
Applied to a goal {A ?- t}, it yields a single subgoal identical to the input,
with the conclusion unaltered and no assumptions added or removed.
{
        A ?- t
     ============  ASSERT_CONCL_TAC t
        A ?- t
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this identity behaviour, on goals with no
assumptions whose conclusions are existentially quantified specification
statements matching the supplied term.

\ENDDOC
